  Name: Talking to the Wind
  Description: 'Lately I''ve been, for a month now, I''m talking to the wind.

    Asking
    them things I no longer want to prevent existing (c''est grammaticalement bancal
    mais c''est pour les rimes)

    All my stiches are opened up, I''m still lying
    on the floor.

    But I though that, life would turn out way more easily"

    "Why
    don''t I seem like myself, when I look through the mirror?

    Why does my cheeks
    seems so stiff, even when no true hunger exists?'
